course: dictionary
lesson: 6312
title: One word, many pieces
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mosaic is a picture or pattern made from lots of small pieces of coloured stone, glass or tile, all fixed side by side. «Rich Romans lived in houses with gardens and mosaics» means the Romans decorated their houses with these small coloured pieces.
explain: The word also has a second meaning. «Canada ... calls itself a mosaic of cultures» means many different cultures are mixed together, like the many pieces that make one picture. The words «a mosaic of» tell you that something is made of many different parts.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Could you say «a picture of cultures»? That does not quite fit. But «a mix of cultures» fits well, so the second meaning is right. Always test your idea in the sentence.
fact: A mosaic is a picture or pattern made from many small pieces of coloured stone, glass or tile.
fact: «Mosaics» in «houses with gardens and mosaics» are decorations made of small coloured pieces, and the Romans made mosaic floors.
fact: «A mosaic of cultures» means many different cultures mixed together to make one whole.
fact: Mosaic is a noun. One picture is a mosaic, and more than one is mosaics.
fact: In maths, mosaics connect with shapes and tiling, where shapes fit together with no gaps.
exercise: «Rich Romans lived in houses with gardens and mosaics.» What is a mosaic here? | *A picture made of many small coloured pieces | A block of flats | A large kind of flat | A type of garden bird
exercise: Canada «calls itself a mosaic of cultures». What does mosaic mean here? | A block of flats | A bright red maple leaf | *Many different cultures mixed together | A single small glass tile
exercise: What is the plural of mosaic? | mosaical | mosaic | *mosaics | mosaicing
test: A Roman mosaic floor is best described as | a cold cloud over a city | a floor made of soft wood | *a floor decorated with small coloured tiles or stones
test: Which sentence uses mosaic the same way as «a mosaic of cultures»? | The mosaic shone in the sun | *Our class is a mosaic of backgrounds and languages | The Romans built a mosaic floor | We made a mosaic of paper squares for art
exam: In «calls itself a mosaic of cultures», which word is the clue that shows the meaning? | The word itself, because it is a short word | The word red | The word calls | *The word cultures, because many different groups of people are mixed together
